  "body": "Stacked on #2279. Retarget this PR to `main` before #2279 merges.\n\n## What changed\n- `setup_align::verified_kind` accepts six more kinds: Drill, Bore, Thread, Circular, Trochoidal Slot and Slot. The refusal message lists them.\n- Slot picks read the setup frame. `slot_bound_of`, `confine_slot` and `slot_from_picks` take the op's setup and use `setup_align::pose_in`. Before, they used `model::transform_of` (the model frame). In an unaligned setup, `pose_in` gives the model pose, so that path does not change.\n- Two old tests used Circular as the refused example. They use 2D Chamfer now (with the `CM-0600-90` chamfer mill).\n- The decision file `docs/decisions/2276-aligned-setup-kinds.md` has a second section.\n\n## Readings\n- Hole recognition (`operation::detect_holes`) reads the material of the op's setup through `setup_align::facets_in`. Thus the hole list of a turned setup is in the setup frame.\n- Circular, Trochoidal Slot and typed Slot take their region and heights from `region_for_job` and `part_aabb_in`, in the setup frame.\n\n## Pinning tests\n`crates/app/tests/setup_align_hole_kinds.rs` (new): a plate with two holes, turned 90 degrees about X and then about Z.\n- `turned_drill_finds_and_cuts_the_holes_of_the_baked_part`\n- `turned_bore_finds_and_cuts_the_holes_of_the_baked_part`\n- `turned_thread_finds_and_cuts_the_holes_of_the_baked_part`\n- `a_hole_list_from_the_turned_setup_never_drills_the_part_as_modelled_silently`\n\n`crates/app/tests/setup_align_2d_kinds.rs`:\n- `turned_circular_cuts_like_the_baked_part`\n- `turned_trochoidal_slot_cuts_like_the_baked_part`\n- `turned_typed_slot_cuts_like_the_baked_part`\n- `turned_picked_slot_fills_the_turned_face`\n- `kinds_without_proof_stay_refused_in_a_turned_setup` (Probe, 2D Chamfer, Deburr)\n\nEach turned case must verify clean, simulate with no gouge, and post the same program as the baked part. The part as modelled must cut a different path or refuse.\n\nAlso run, all green: `setup_align`, `opframe_picks`, `slot_pick_refusals`, `slot_picks`. Clippy `-D warnings` is clean on the lib and these test targets. `cargo fmt --check` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The quick tier as one run. I ran the touched suites one by one.\n- Thread on external bosses. The test threads holes only.\n- Circular and Trochoidal Slot from picks. The tests use typed coordinates.\n- A picked Slot that cuts into material. The picked Slot test cuts in air above the part; the proof is the seeded XY.\n- The UI panels in a turned setup.\n\n## Kinds still refused\n- 2D Chamfer: #2283\n- Deburr: #2284\n- Probe: #2285\n- 5-axis and rotary kinds: #2286\n- Non-mill machines: #2287\n\nThe verify check and the post gate do not change.\n\nChangelog: Drill, Bore, Thread, Circular, Trochoidal Slot and Slot operations now generate in a setup that holds the part turned (part alignment); picked Slot faces and edges are read in the setup frame.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nRefs #2276\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
